  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The session calendar and task board can show both attendance and the work affected by an absence.\", \"decision\": \"How should volunteers announce a change in their plans?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers notify a coordinator who updates attendance and affected tasks together. One shared update keeps the two records aligned.\nVolunteers arrange cover for affected tasks on the board and then update calendar attendance. Responsibility is transferred before the attendance change is finalized.\nVolunteers update their calendar attendance and then mark affected tasks on the board. The work change follows the announced absence."
    }
